  "full_text": "Yeah, when I was a kid, right, I had, let's see, I got a birthmark on my right knee. Hold on a second. So I got a birthmark. There's my birthmark. So, anyway. So, yeah, I was very self-conscious, you know, as a kid. A bit nasty, right? So, like. You know, a beauty mark, I've heard of a beauty mark. That's like a mole on someone's face or something. Maybe it's like, makes them humble, you know. Yeah, humble. And maybe that's beautiful, you know. I don't know. That kind of made me, I didn't have an attitude, that's for sure. So like, anyway. Oh no, I got a birthmark. So like, wasn't particularly fond of wearing shorts. But I went to, the Jill Rutledge years, I was in the swimming pool a lot, you know. But anyway, so. So, the mark of the beast. So like, what's his face? What's his face? Gorbachev has a birthmark. All things considered, it's a pretty well-ordered birthmark. It's nice and round, nice shape to it. Terry, you're part nigger. Yeah, I'm about, uh... How much nigger blood you got? I don't know. Let me count.",
